// The cobaia go module marker (the goget wave): the
// documentation envelope rides the go get rung the way it rides the
// maven, nuget, rubygems and gradle rungs — the module path answers the
// github.com/wenathlan/devthink monorepo with the per-application
// subdirectory and the major version suffix the go semver law demands
// at the v2 line, and the version answers the per-application tag
// (cobaia/vX.Y.Z on the release commit) the publish lane syncs — the go
// module registry carries no version literal the rung ladder would have
// to stamp, the same way the gradle marker reads the envelope
// package.json at build time.
